[Unit]
Description=Check that HDW4S can hand out a desktop and that every running session publishes its own identity
Documentation=man:hdw4s(8)

[Service]
ExecStart=/usr/lib/hdw4s/hdw4s check
Type=oneshot

# Deliberately no LogLevelMax=, unlike hdw4s-reaper.service. That one runs every
# few minutes and says nothing worth keeping; this one says nothing at all until
# something is wrong, and the text it prints then names the slot and the repair.
# Filtering it to warning would drop exactly the output this unit exists to
# produce, and leave only "failed", which points at no slot.
#
# The failure IS the signal: "hdw4s check" exits non-zero, systemd marks the
# unit failed, and "systemctl --failed" names it. Nothing here restarts a
# session -- a check that quietly repaired what it found would be one nobody
# ever read, and the thing worth knowing is that a slot was running without the
# publisher for two hours, not that it has now been bounced.
